Package: axlisten
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Tom Fanning <tom@m0lte.uk>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Suggests: axcall
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/packet-net/axcall
Description: AX.25 channel monitor over KISS
 Shows every AX.25 frame a TNC hears, decoded: addresses and digipeaters,
 frame type, sequence numbers, and what the frame carries. Text is shown as
 text; APRS, NET/ROM (with routing broadcasts), IP and ARP as a summary. Listens on any number of ports at once, and reopens a port
 that goes away. JSON output is there for programs.
 .
 --classic gives the output and the options of the axlisten from ax25-apps,
 for scripts and log parsers written against it.
 .
 Receive only: it never transmits and needs no callsign. It carries its own
 AX.25 decoding and speaks KISS to a TNC over a serial port or over TCP, so it
 needs no kernel AX.25 stack and no privilege.
 .
 Self-contained: bundles its own .NET runtime, so no system runtime is
 required.
